A child can withdraw the contributions to a custodial Roth IRA (the dollars originally put in) at any time without the early-withdrawal tax. Earnings taken out before age 59 1/2 are different: they can be taxable, and the [IRS adds a 10% additional tax](https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc557) on the part of the distribution included in gross income, on top of regular income tax. The IRS sets out the full rules for Roth distributions in [Publication 590-B](https://www.irs.gov/publications/p590b).